---
import Container from "../components/Container.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import SectionHeader from "../components/SectionHeader.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout title="Privacy — Conclave AX" description="How Conclave AX separates identity, Project collaboration, local execution, AI Accounts, and public-site telemetry.">
  <Section>
    <Container>
      <SectionHeader eyebrow="Privacy" title="Privacy follows the same boundaries as the product." description="Conclave AX is designed so collaboration, execution capacity, and external AI credentials can be authorized independently." headingLevel={1} />
      <div class="legal-content">
        <h2>Human identity and Projects</h2>
        <p>Conclave Cloud authenticates people and applies Project membership and role checks to shared collaboration data such as Workstreams, discussions, Runs, artifacts, and Project settings. Joining a Project does not make another person's execution Workspace or private AI Accounts generally available.</p>

        <h2>Workspaces and local execution</h2>
        <p>A Workspace represents an execution environment controlled by its owner. A Project can use that environment only through an explicit Workspace grant that defines allowed execution scope. Local repository access and Worker processes remain subject to Workspace runtime controls.</p>

        <h2>AI Accounts</h2>
        <p>AI Accounts represent external provider identities. They are private by default and are authorized independently from Workspace access. Sharing an Account authorizes eligible use; it does not expose the underlying plaintext credential to Project collaborators.</p>

        <h2>Workers and assignment data</h2>
        <p>Workers receive scoped assignment context needed for their task rather than Conclave user sessions or unrestricted machine credentials. Execution history may include task metadata, results, artifacts, findings, usage, and evidence needed to operate and audit the workflow.</p>

        <h2>Public website</h2>
        <p>This public website uses minimal, same-origin operational telemetry and does not provide a place to submit AI credentials, private repository content, or Workspace secrets.</p>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>
</SiteLayout>
